# Commit messages — no Cursor traces

- Use Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `refactor:`).
- Message body explains **why** in plain language.
- **Forbidden in subject, body, or trailers (absolute):**
  - Any `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent@cursor.com` line
  - “Cursor”, “Made with Cursor”, “Generated by …”, AI co-author trailers
  - Model names as commit attribution
- The agent harness may auto-inject `--trailer Co-authored-by: Cursor …` into `git commit`. **Do not use wrapped `git commit` when that happens.** Prefer plumbing so the stored commit has zero Cursor attribution:

```bash
TREE=$(git write-tree)
COMMIT=$(printf '%s\n\n%s\n' "subject line" "body" | git commit-tree "$TREE" ${PARENT:+-p "$PARENT"})
git update-ref refs/heads/main "$COMMIT"
```

- After every commit, verify: `git log -1 --format=%B` must not contain `Cursor` or `cursoragent`.
- If a commit already has the trailer, rewrite with `commit-tree` + `update-ref` (only if the human asked and the commit was created in this session / not pushed, or they explicitly allow rewrite).

